# Routing - web

## i18n

Routes live under `[lang]/` (`en`, `pl`, …). `/` and `/en` redirect → `/en/home`.

## Page convention

Marketing URLs share one catch-all that hydrates the shell from CMS:

```vue
<!-- web/src/pages/[lang]/[slug].vue -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { useRoute } from 'nuxt/app'
import { computed } from 'vue'
import { usePublicShellPage } from '../../composables/use_public_shell_page'

const route = useRoute()
const slug = computed(() => String(route.params.slug || ''))
await usePublicShellPage(slug)
</script>
<template><div /></template>
```

Section SFCs live under `web/src/sections/`. SEO title/description come from the published page in admin (with hardcoded fallbacks for known marketing slugs).

## API

`web/src/server/api/[...slug].ts` → `dispatchSupabaseApiGateway` from `shared_modules/nuc_api`.
